# Binaries — the build artifact is produced by deploy/build.ps1, never committed.
# ANCHORED to the repo root with a leading slash, deliberately: the unanchored form
# `sitectl` also matched the SOURCE DIRECTORY cmd/sitectl/, which silently kept
# cmd/sitectl/main.go — the program's entire entry point — untracked from C1 until
# 2026-08-19. A fresh clone had no main package and could not build. Do not remove
# these leading slashes.
*.exe
/sitectl
/sitectl-*
bin/
dist/

# Databases — self-created at runtime, never committed
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Local/secret config — a post's site.toml / config.toml holds its login password
# and peer key: never commit one. Only the secret-free plan example is committed.
site.toml
config.toml
*.local.toml
.env
passwords.txt
IT-CHECKLIST.txt
